ATCCardsData("EN02C1",[["ij45ct","C1 word (verb): to make something happen faster or earlier (starts with \"acc\")","accelerate (acelerar). Example: \"The new radar system should accelerate the handover between sectors.\""],["vex35c","C1 word (adj): responsible for your actions and expected to explain them (starts with \"acc\")","accountable (responsable ante alguien). Example: \"Controllers are accountable for the safety of every aircraft in their sector.\""],["470adv","C1 word (verb): to gradually get more and more of something over time (starts with \"acc\")","accumulate (acumular). Example: \"Ice can accumulate on the wings during a long descent through cloud.\""],["1vqv852","C1 word (verb): to stick to a rule, belief or plan (starts with \"adh\")","adhere (to) (adherirse, cumplir). Example: \"All pilots must adhere to the published departure procedure.\""],["vhgc9y","C1 word (adj): next to or very near something else (starts with \"adj\")","adjacent (adyacente, contiguo). Example: \"The two adjacent sectors share a common frequency.\""],["o89opw","C1 word (adj): harmful or unfavourable (starts with \"adv\")","adverse (adverso). Example: \"Adverse weather forced the airport to close for two hours.\""],["6qjq3d","C1 word (conj): formal word meaning \"although\" or \"even though\" (starts with \"alb\")","albeit (aunque, si bien). Example: \"The delay was short, albeit costly.\""],["1wstazr","C1 word (verb): to give something officially to a person or purpose (resources, time, money) (starts with \"all\")","allocate (asignar, destinar). Example: \"The supervisor will allocate the new slots to the busiest routes.\""],["ox2lon","C1 word (verb): to change the words of a text or law slightly to improve it (starts with \"ame\")","amend (modificar, enmendar). Example: \"The regulation was amended to include drones.\""],["zmd69m","C1 word (prep): in the middle of something, usually a difficult situation (starts with \"ami\")","amid (en medio de). Example: \"Amid growing concern about noise, the airport changed its routes.\""],["c6tupc","C1 word (noun): the equipment or tools needed for a particular purpose (starts with \"app\")","apparatus (aparato, equipo). Example: \"The breathing apparatus was checked before the drill.\""],["15bbto4","C1 word (adj): decided by chance or personal whim rather than by a system or reason (starts with \"arb\")","arbitrary (arbitrario). Example: \"The choice of runway was not arbitrary; it depended on the wind.\""],["1cp1mjv","C1 word (verb): to express ideas or feelings clearly in words (starts with \"art\")","articulate (articular, expresar con claridad). Example: \"She could articulate complex ideas under pressure.\""],["q4k9bv","C1 word (verb): to state something firmly and confidently (starts with \"ass\")","assert (afirmar, sostener). Example: \"He asserted that the report was accurate.\""],["7nfw4b","C1 word (verb): to succeed in getting something, usually after effort (starts with \"att\")","attain (alcanzar, lograr). Example: \"The aircraft attained its cruising level after 20 minutes.\""],["5y29jc","C1 word (verb): to give official permission for something (starts with \"aut\")","authorize (autorizar). Example: \"Only the duty manager can authorize a change of runway.\""],["1sgm0ve","C1 word (verb, formal): to wait for something (starts with \"awa\")","await (esperar, aguardar). Example: \"The crew awaited clearance to push back.\""],["lby6vi","C1 word (noun): a failure to obey a rule or law; also a gap in a wall or defence (starts with \"bre\")","breach (incumplimiento, brecha). Example: \"Flying without clearance is a serious breach of regulations.\""],["1ljefby","C1 word (noun): the main or largest part of something (starts with \"bul\")","bulk (la mayor parte, volumen). Example: \"The bulk of the traffic arrives between 07:00 and 09:00.\""],["17z2sym","C1 word (noun): a heavy responsibility, load or duty (starts with \"bur\")","burden (carga, peso). Example: \"Automation reduced the burden on the controllers.\""],["1ec2khl","C1 word (noun): the ability to do something (starts with \"cap\")","capability (capacidad, aptitud). Example: \"The airport has the capability to handle wide-body aircraft.\""],["1wixtve","C1 word (noun): great care to avoid danger or mistakes (starts with \"cau\")","caution (precaución, cautela). Example: \"Proceed with caution; the runway may be wet.\""],["1a7oohu","C1 word (verb, formal): to stop or come to an end (starts with \"cea\")","cease (cesar). Example: \"All flights ceased when the volcanic ash reached the coast.\""],["dz66r7","C1 word (noun): the quality of being clear and easy to understand (starts with \"cla\")","clarity (claridad). Example: \"Clarity is more important than speed on the radio.\""],["5cpeot","C1 word (verb): to happen at the same time as something else (starts with \"coi\")","coincide (coincidir). Example: \"The strike coincided with the busiest weekend of the year.\""],["xisq5u","C1 word (verb): to work together with someone to produce something (starts with \"col\")","collaborate (colaborar). Example: \"Pilots and controllers must collaborate closely during a diversion.\""],["wys4z1","C1 word (verb, formal): to begin (starts with \"com\")","commence (comenzar). Example: \"The exercise will commence at 09:00.\""],["aoo8k4","C1 word (verb): to force someone to do something (starts with \"com\")","compel (obligar, forzar). Example: \"Bad weather compelled the crew to divert.\""],["12i0ozu","C1 word (verb): to give someone money or something to balance a loss or injury (starts with \"com\")","compensate (compensar, indemnizar). Example: \"Airlines must compensate passengers for long delays.\""],["1skf5rj","C1 word (verb): to obey a rule, order or request (starts with \"com\")","comply (with) (cumplir con). Example: \"Aircraft must comply with air traffic instructions.\""],["1w5hxux","C1 word (verb): to hide something or keep it secret (starts with \"con\")","conceal (ocultar). Example: \"He tried to conceal his mistake from the supervisor.\""],["1vjgq0f","C1 word (verb): to admit that something is true, often reluctantly (starts with \"con\")","concede (admitir, conceder). Example: \"The airline conceded that the delay was avoidable.\""],["15legmv","C1 word (adj): following one after another without a break (starts with \"con\")","consecutive (consecutivo, seguido). Example: \"She worked five consecutive night shifts.\""],["nxngbt","C1 word (noun): a general agreement among a group (starts with \"con\")","consensus (consenso). Example: \"There is a consensus that the procedure needs revising.\""],["q4exmh","C1 word (noun): something that limits what you can do (starts with \"con\")","constraint (restricción, limitación). Example: \"Budget constraints delayed the new tower.\""],["1n5dzdo","C1 word (verb): to argue or claim that something is true (starts with \"con\")","contend (sostener, afirmar; also: competir). Example: \"The union contends that the rosters are unsafe.\""],["1paex5q","C1 word (noun): a statement or fact that is the opposite of, or inconsistent with, another (starts with \"con\")","contradiction (contradicción). Example: \"There is a contradiction between the two reports.\""],["tnpdoi","C1 word (verb): to match, be similar to, or be equal to something; also to exchange letters (starts with \"cor\")","correspond (corresponder; escribirse). Example: \"The figures on the chart do not correspond to the data table.\""],["ktyjlv","C1 word (adj): able to be believed or trusted (starts with \"cre\")","credible (creíble). Example: \"The controller gave a credible explanation of the event.\""],["1iceu5w","C1 word (verb, formal): to consider or judge something in a particular way (starts with \"dee\")","deem (considerar, juzgar). Example: \"The runway was deemed unsafe after the inspection.\""],["l0qyq","C1 word (noun): a lack of something that is needed (starts with \"def\")","deficiency (deficiencia, carencia). Example: \"The audit found a deficiency in the training records.\""],["44f2nc","C1 word (adj): easily damaged or broken; needing careful handling (starts with \"del\")","delicate (delicado). Example: \"Negotiations over the airspace change were delicate.\""],["1rgzlh6","C1 word (verb): to move troops, equipment or resources into position for use (starts with \"dep\")","deploy (desplegar). Example: \"Emergency crews were deployed along the runway.\""],["rszrjc","C1 word (verb): to become worse (starts with \"det\")","deteriorate (deteriorarse, empeorar). Example: \"Visibility deteriorated rapidly after midday.\""],["jrlf3l","C1 word (verb): to invent or plan a method or system (starts with \"dev\")","devise (idear, concebir). Example: \"The team devised a new way to sequence arrivals.\""],["m65fcp","C1 word (verb): to become or make smaller, weaker or less important (starts with \"dim\")","diminish (disminuir). Example: \"Fatigue can diminish a controller's alertness.\""],["13iy8v3","C1 word (verb): to throw away something you no longer need (starts with \"dis\")","discard (desechar, descartar). Example: \"Discard any charts that are out of date.\""],["ychdu9","C1 word (noun): the freedom or right to decide what to do; also tact (starts with \"dis\")","discretion (discreción; libertad de decisión). Example: \"The supervisor may use their discretion in exceptional cases.\""],["1c2osxc","C1 word (verb): to interrupt or stop the normal course of something (starts with \"dis\")","disrupt (interrumpir, perturbar). Example: \"A power cut disrupted all radar displays.\""],["1on79an","C1 word (verb): to change the shape, sound or meaning of something so that it is not accurate (starts with \"dis\")","distort (distorsionar, deformar). Example: \"Interference can distort the audio signal.\""],["1v2h0j6","C1 word (verb): to change the direction or use of something (starts with \"div\")","divert (desviar). Example: \"Three flights were diverted to Valencia.\""],["ms2ui0","C1 word (adj): consisting of two parts or having two purposes (starts with \"dua\")","dual (doble, dual). Example: \"The airport has a dual role as a civil and military base.\""],["89d3y1","C1 word (adj): very detailed and complicated (starts with \"ela\")","elaborate (elaborado, complejo). Example: \"The airline had an elaborate contingency plan.\""],["1ftu7pq","C1 word (adj): qualified or allowed to do or receive something (starts with \"eli\")","eligible (apto, con derecho a). Example: \"Candidates must be eligible to work in the EU.\""],["1peip7h","C1 word (verb): to begin a journey or a new venture (starts with \"emb\")","embark (embarcar; emprender). Example: \"She embarked on a career in air traffic control.\""],["gr15rx","C1 word (verb): to include a wide range of things (starts with \"enc\")","encompass (abarcar, englobar). Example: \"The course encompasses navigation, meteorology and law.\""],["1k73yht","C1 word (verb): to make people obey a law or rule (starts with \"enf\")","enforce (hacer cumplir). Example: \"The authority enforces safety regulations.\""],["1sm1641","C1 word (verb, formal): to happen afterwards, especially as a result (starts with \"ens\")","ensue (sobrevenir, derivarse). Example: \"Chaos ensued when the system crashed.\""],["uy26xr","C1 word (verb): to increase in intensity or seriousness (starts with \"esc\")","escalate (intensificarse, escalar). Example: \"The dispute escalated into a full strike.\""],["bjw4tl","C1 word (verb): to move people from a dangerous place to a safe one (starts with \"eva\")","evacuate (evacuar). Example: \"The terminal was evacuated after the alarm.\""],["nmhzfk","C1 word (verb): to use effort, force or influence (starts with \"exe\")","exert (ejercer). Example: \"The passengers exerted pressure on the airline to compensate them.\""],["1hcyzod","C1 word (adj): stated clearly and in detail, leaving no doubt (starts with \"exp\")","explicit (explícito). Example: \"The clearance was explicit: hold short of runway 24.\""],["d58o4a","C1 word (verb): to make an action or process easier (starts with \"fac\")","facilitate (facilitar). Example: \"New software facilitates the flow of traffic.\""],["lc5l6j","C1 word (noun): a fault or mistake that makes something less good (starts with \"fla\")","flaw (defecto, fallo). Example: \"A flaw in the design caused the crack.\""],["1qsfa71","C1 word (verb): to be successful, grow or develop well (starts with \"flo\")","flourish (florecer, prosperar). Example: \"Regional airports flourished after the reform.\""],["1yfzf5k","C1 word (verb): to develop and prepare a plan or idea in detail (starts with \"for\")","formulate (formular). Example: \"The ministry is formulating a new aviation strategy.\""],["667ym0","C1 word (verb): to encourage the development of something (starts with \"fos\")","foster (fomentar, promover). Example: \"The programme fosters cooperation between agencies.\""],["xp4nek","C1 word (adj): easily broken or damaged (starts with \"fra\")","fragile (frágil). Example: \"The recovery of air traffic remains fragile.\""],["eoldnc","C1 word (noun): help, advice or direction given to someone (starts with \"gui\")","guidance (orientación, guía). Example: \"The pilot followed the controller's guidance to the gate.\""],["apbsy1","C1 word (verb): to stop; to make something stop (starts with \"hal\")","halt (detener, parar). Example: \"All departures were halted because of the lightning.\""],["11cr8fu","C1 word (noun): something that may cause danger or harm (starts with \"haz\")","hazard (peligro, riesgo). Example: \"Birds are a serious hazard near the runway.\""],["7dt7j8","C1 word (verb): to make something stronger or more intense (starts with \"hei\")","heighten (aumentar, intensificar). Example: \"The accident heightened concerns about fatigue.\""],["k98bl4","C1 word (noun): a system of ranks, from top to bottom, in an organization (starts with \"hie\")","hierarchy (jerarquía). Example: \"The flat hierarchy in the cockpit encourages challenge and feedback.\""],["cvkb7l","C1 word (adj): about to happen very soon, usually something unpleasant (starts with \"imm\")","imminent (inminente). Example: \"A thunderstorm was imminent.\""],["59rlx1","C1 word (noun): the process of putting a plan or decision into action (starts with \"imp\")","implementation (implantación, puesta en práctica). Example: \"The implementation of the new procedure begins in March.\""],["tk6pwy","C1 word (adj): not enough in quantity or quality (starts with \"ina\")","inadequate (inadecuado, insuficiente). Example: \"Their preparation was inadequate for such weather.\""],["zqwzr3","C1 word (verb): to make someone or something responsible for a cost, or to suffer something unpleasant as a result of your actions (starts with \"inc\")","incur (incurrir en, acarrear). Example: \"The airline incurred heavy costs during the strike.\""],["1vaspg","C1 word (adj): belonging naturally to something as a permanent part (starts with \"inh\")","inherent (inherente). Example: \"Some risk is inherent in every flight.\""],["11hmjgp","C1 word (verb): to make something begin (starts with \"ini\")","initiate (iniciar, dar comienzo a). Example: \"The captain initiated a go-around.\""],["80hfty","C1 word (verb): to get involved in a situation in order to change or help (starts with \"int\")","intervene (intervenir). Example: \"The supervisor intervened to resolve the conflict.\""],["r6zuna","C1 word (adj): not damaged or complete (starts with \"int\")","intact (intacto). Example: \"The black box was found intact.\""],["1id5eyx","C1 word (adj): essential and forming a necessary part of a whole (starts with \"int\")","integral (integral, fundamental). Example: \"Teamwork is integral to safe air traffic control.\""],["cuj1y2","C1 word (noun): being honest and having strong moral principles (starts with \"int\")","integrity (integridad). Example: \"The investigation was conducted with complete integrity.\""],["11zegj4","C1 word (verb): to get involved and prevent something from happening or spoil it (starts with \"int\")","interfere (interferir; entrometerse). Example: \"Radio noise interfered with the transmission.\""],["rhv0aa","C1 word (adj): happening between two events or periods; temporary (starts with \"int\")","interim (provisional, interino). Example: \"An interim report was published in June.\""],["ykv4wc","C1 word (verb): to ask for or use a law or authority to justify or support an action (starts with \"inv\")","invoke (invocar). Example: \"The captain invoked emergency authority.\""],["13ghei0","C1 word (adj): not connected with what is being discussed (starts with \"irr\")","irrelevant (irrelevante). Example: \"Information that is irrelevant to the task should be ignored.\""],["1rbo838","C1 word (noun): the power or right to make legal decisions over a particular area (starts with \"jur\")","jurisdiction (jurisdicción). Example: \"Each state has jurisdiction over its own airspace.\""],["9cna8f","C1 word (noun): the possibility that something will happen (starts with \"lik\")","likelihood (probabilidad). Example: \"The likelihood of a collision is extremely small.\""],["2ot77o","C1 word (adj): legally allowed or based on good reasons (starts with \"leg\")","legitimate (legítimo). Example: \"There were legitimate reasons for the delay.\""],["1iu28eu","C1 word (adj): legally responsible for something (starts with \"lia\")","liable (responsable; propenso). Example: \"The operator is liable for damage to the airport.\""],["118nqnt","C1 word (adj): required by law or rules; compulsory (starts with \"man\")","mandatory (obligatorio). Example: \"It is mandatory to read back runway clearances.\""],["zr9bzb","C1 word (noun): the size or importance of something (starts with \"mag\")","magnitude (magnitud). Example: \"Nobody expected the magnitude of the disruption.\""],["1iu6sfd","C1 word (noun): the work of keeping a machine or building in good condition (starts with \"mai\")","maintenance (mantenimiento). Example: \"The aircraft is undergoing scheduled maintenance.\""],["1gk5k5r","C1 word (verb): to join together to form a bigger organization (starts with \"mer\")","merge (fusionar, confluir). Example: \"The two companies merged last year.\""],["o5p5j3","C1 word (adj): very small in amount; the least possible (starts with \"min\")","minimal (mínimo). Example: \"Delays were minimal despite the snow.\""],["1vlm4n9","C1 word (adj): giving a wrong or false idea (starts with \"mis\")","misleading (engañoso). Example: \"The label was misleading.\""],["1ghxn6e","C1 word (adj): felt or done by two or more people in the same way (starts with \"mut\")","mutual (mutuo). Example: \"Trust must be mutual between pilot and controller.\""],["1dx2te8","C1 word (adv): that is to say (starts with \"nam\")","namely (a saber, es decir). Example: \"Two runways are affected, namely 06 and 24.\""],["1ytg69","C1 word (adv): despite what has just been said (starts with \"non\")","nonetheless (no obstante, sin embargo). Example: \"The forecast was poor; nonetheless, the flight departed.\""],["41fvb3","C1 word (verb): to formally tell someone about something (starts with \"not\")","notify (notificar). Example: \"The pilot notified the tower of a bird strike.\""],["1hxvofq","C1 word (verb): to make someone legally or morally obliged to do something (starts with \"obl\")","oblige (obligar). Example: \"Airlines are obliged to publish delay statistics.\""],["1hhqubt","C1 word (noun): an event or something that happens (starts with \"occ\")","occurrence (suceso, ocurrencia). Example: \"Every occurrence must be reported.\""],["f0p0qn","C1 word (adj): relating to how something works; in use (starts with \"ope\")","operational (operativo, en funcionamiento). Example: \"The new radar is fully operational.\""],["1fiycce","C1 word (verb): to watch and manage a situation or group of workers (starts with \"ove\")","oversee (supervisar). Example: \"A senior controller oversees the training.\""],["1wskrmk","C1 word (verb): to not notice something, or to ignore it (starts with \"ove\")","overlook (pasar por alto). Example: \"It is easy to overlook a small detail in a long checklist.\""],["1s58xo3","C1 word (verb): to persist or continue to exist (starts with \"per\")","persist (persistir). Example: \"The fog is expected to persist until noon.\""],["19x22e3","C1 word (noun): the people who work for an organization (starts with \"per\")","personnel (personal, plantilla). Example: \"Only authorized personnel may enter the tower.\""],["kcul47","C1 word (verb): to arrange for something to take place at a later time (starts with \"pos\")","postpone (aplazar). Example: \"The flight was postponed until the storm passed.\""],["1yu13jf","C1 word (noun): an earlier example that can be used to justify a later decision (starts with \"pre\")","precedent (precedente). Example: \"The ruling set a precedent for later cases.\""],["tby40n","C1 word (noun): the quality of being exact and accurate (starts with \"pre\")","precision (precisión). Example: \"The approach requires precision.\""],["1olqiq1","C1 word (adj): coming before the main event; introductory (starts with \"pre\")","preliminary (preliminar). Example: \"Preliminary results suggest a technical fault.\""],["c95ev9","C1 word (verb): to suppose that something is true without proof (starts with \"pre\")","presume (suponer, presumir). Example: \"I presume you have checked the weather.\""],["150ykfc","C1 word (verb, formal): to be the most common or widespread; also to win (starts with \"pre\")","prevail (prevalecer, predominar). Example: \"Calm conditions prevailed all week.\""],["o5ilrj","C1 word (adj): important, well known (starts with \"pro\")","prominent (destacado, prominente). Example: \"A prominent landmark helps VFR pilots navigate.\""],["as5ukg","C1 word (adj): very great, deep or intense (starts with \"pro\")","profound (profundo). Example: \"The accident had a profound effect on safety culture.\""],["2he4eh","C1 word (verb): to deliberately cause a reaction, often anger (starts with \"pro\")","provoke (provocar). Example: \"The announcement provoked a strike.\""],["910zra","C1 word (noun): a set of rules for correct procedure or behaviour (starts with \"pro\")","protocol (protocolo). Example: \"The emergency protocol was followed to the letter.\""],["xcr3zb","C1 word (noun): the act of supplying something; a condition in an agreement (starts with \"pro\")","provision (provisión; cláusula). Example: \"The contract makes provision for overtime.\""],["1ybvkws","C1 word (verb): to continue after a pause (starts with \"res\")","resume (reanudar). Example: \"Normal operations will resume at 14:00.\""],["ps876n","C1 word (adj): unwilling and therefore slow to do something (starts with \"rel\")","reluctant (reacio, reticente). Example: \"The captain was reluctant to accept a tailwind landing.\""],["q78cek","C1 word (adj): strong and unlikely to fail (starts with \"rob\")","robust (robusto, sólido). Example: \"The system needs robust backup procedures.\""],["122qcel","C1 word (noun): the range of things that a subject or activity covers (starts with \"sco\")","scope (alcance, ámbito). Example: \"The scope of the review is limited to en-route control.\""],["j0jp9c","C1 word (noun): careful and detailed examination (starts with \"scr\")","scrutiny (escrutinio). Example: \"The incident came under intense scrutiny.\""],["1azt66x","C1 word (verb): to take hold of something suddenly and with force; also to take by legal authority (starts with \"sei\")","seize (agarrar; incautar). Example: \"The authorities seized the documents.\""],["zq08sm","C1 word (adj): important and large in amount (starts with \"sub\")","substantial (sustancial, considerable). Example: \"A substantial number of flights were cancelled.\""],["wmqkbs","C1 word (adj): not obvious; delicate and hard to notice (starts with \"sub\")","subtle (sutil). Example: \"A subtle change in engine noise alerted the pilot.\""],["85xvl3","C1 word (verb): to be in charge of and watch over a person or activity (starts with \"sup\")","supervise (supervisar). Example: \"Trainee controllers are supervised by an instructor.\""],["1ecbqan","C1 word (verb): to stop something from continuing or being seen (starts with \"sup\")","suppress (suprimir, reprimir). Example: \"The fire suppression system activated automatically.\""],["34947j","C1 word (adj): direct and easy to understand or do (starts with \"str\")","straightforward (sencillo, directo). Example: \"The procedure is straightforward.\""],["te2jfw","C1 word (noun): pressure or worry caused by too much work or difficulty (starts with \"str\")","strain (tensión, presión). Example: \"Night shifts put a strain on the body.\""],["1jiuu29","C1 word (adj): relating to a plan for achieving a long-term goal (starts with \"str\")","strategic (estratégico). Example: \"The strategic plan covers the next ten years.\""],["1lnsr05","C1 word (noun): the state of being steady and not likely to change (starts with \"sta\")","stability (estabilidad). Example: \"The aircraft's stability was affected by turbulence.\""],["1i8cv0e","C1 word (noun): a large number or amount that is more than needed (starts with \"sur\")","surplus (excedente). Example: \"The airline had a surplus of pilots.\""],["1oewu2d","C1 word (verb): to give up or hand over control (starts with \"sur\")","surrender (rendirse, ceder). Example: \"The aircraft surrendered its slot.\""],["8osi4d","C1 word (adv): according to what people believe or say, although it may not be true (starts with \"sup\")","supposedly (supuestamente). Example: \"The runway was supposedly closed for repairs.\""],["sd4gb","C1 word (adj): easily hurt, attacked or damaged (starts with \"vul\")","vulnerable (vulnerable). Example: \"Small aircraft are vulnerable to wake turbulence.\""],["k9ikqv","C1 word (noun): the quality of being trustworthy and performing consistently well (starts with \"rel\")","reliability (fiabilidad). Example: \"The reliability of the engines is well documented.\""],["1w7t6lq","Collocation: \"to ___ a decision\" (take/make/do)? Which verb is preferred in standard British English?","make a decision (tomar una decisión). Also \"take a decision\" is common in British English. Not \"do a decision\"."],["1kokmfo","Collocation: \"to ___ a risk\"","take a risk (correr un riesgo). Not \"make a risk\"."],["1ec442r","Collocation: \"to ___ progress\"","make progress (hacer progresos). Not \"do progress\"."],["1kz1u93","Collocation: \"to ___ an effort\"","make an effort (hacer un esfuerzo). Not \"do an effort\"."],["tw6ehb","Collocation: \"to ___ a mistake\"","make a mistake (cometer un error). Not \"do a mistake\"."],["67lwc9","Collocation: \"to ___ damage\"","do damage (causar daño): \"The storm did serious damage.\" Also \"cause damage\"."],["1ekroua","Collocation: \"to ___ somebody a favour\"","do somebody a favour (hacerle un favor a alguien)."],["raibol","Collocation: \"to ___ research\"","do research / carry out research (investigar). Not \"make research\"."],["fbn34w","Collocation: \"to ___ a conclusion\"","draw a conclusion / reach a conclusion (llegar a una conclusión). Not \"make a conclusion\"."],["195k7qb","Collocation: \"to ___ attention to\" something","pay attention to (prestar atención a). Not \"give\" or \"put\" attention."],["12p05ed","Collocation: \"to ___ a lesson\"","learn a lesson (aprender la lección) / teach somebody a lesson (darle una lección a alguien)."],["7w5y28","Collocation: \"a ___ deadline\" (adjective for a date that cannot be moved)","tight deadline (plazo ajustado). Also \"meet a deadline\" (cumplir un plazo)."],["1opjgm9","Collocation: \"to ___ a deadline\"","meet a deadline (cumplir un plazo). Also: miss a deadline (no cumplirlo)."],["ge6r3w","Collocation: \"a ___ rain\" (very heavy)","heavy rain (lluvia intensa). Not \"strong rain\"."],["1lyu6y1","Collocation: \"a ___ wind\" (very powerful)","strong wind (viento fuerte). Not \"heavy wind\". Note: heavy rain, strong wind."],["1tai29s","Collocation: \"___ traffic\" (a lot of vehicles or aircraft)","heavy traffic (tráfico denso). Also \"light traffic\" (poco tráfico)."],["1dk5xxa","Collocation: \"a ___ chance\" (very small)","slim chance / faint chance (una posibilidad remota)."],["yntpgk","Collocation: \"to ___ a complaint\"","lodge / file / make a complaint (presentar una queja)."],["ciq9so","Collocation: \"to ___ an opportunity\"","seize / take / miss an opportunity (aprovechar / perder una oportunidad)."],["u14x2d","Collocation: \"to ___ a role\"","play a role (desempeñar un papel). Also \"play a part\"."],["1ex8b3l","Collocation: \"to ___ a stand\" (take a position)","take a stand (adoptar una postura firme)."],["11t56z8","Collocation: \"to ___ a toll\" (cause harm or loss)","take a toll (on): \"Night shifts take a toll on your health.\" (pasar factura)"],["16dsyt9","Collocation: \"to ___ to a halt\"","come to a halt / grind to a halt (detenerse por completo)."],["mzgxe4","Collocation: \"to ___ a matter of urgency\" (adverb-noun pair): \"This is a ___ priority.\"","top priority (máxima prioridad). Also \"high priority\" (alta prioridad)."],["amlm3d","Collocation: \"___ evidence\" (facts that prove something)","compelling / strong / conclusive evidence (pruebas contundentes). Not \"big evidence\"."],["6kr09d","Collocation: \"___ awareness\" (a good understanding of a situation)","situational awareness (conciencia situacional): a key term in aviation human factors."],["mhy65o","Collocation: \"to raise ___\" (make people notice a problem)","raise awareness (concienciar, sensibilizar). Also \"raise concerns\", \"raise a question\"."],["1hx0z34","Collocation: \"to ___ a problem\" (deal with it)","tackle / address / solve / resolve a problem (abordar / resolver un problema)."],["1qyz9na","Collocation: \"to ___ a concern\" (feel worried)","have / express / share a concern (about); \"voice concerns\" (expresar preocupación)."],["wrt2w2","Collocation: \"a ___ of evidence\" (some pieces of evidence)","piece of evidence (una prueba). \"Evidence\" is uncountable: never \"an evidence\" or \"evidences\"."],["1574s4d","Collocation: \"a ___ of advice\"","piece of advice (un consejo). \"Advice\" is uncountable: never \"an advice\" or \"advices\"."],["psro6p","Collocation: \"a ___ of information\"","piece / item of information (un dato). \"Information\" is uncountable: never \"informations\"."],["b3moj4","Collocation: \"a ___ of news\"","piece of news / a news item (una noticia). \"News\" is uncountable and takes a singular verb."],["n0jx6v","Collocation: \"to ___ a speech / a presentation\"","give / deliver a speech or presentation (dar un discurso / una presentación). Not \"do a speech\"."],["1jd84bn","Collocation: \"to ___ a bill\" (pay)","settle / pay a bill (saldar una factura). Also \"foot the bill\"."],["810kab","Collocation: \"to ___ a gap\"","bridge / fill / close a gap (salvar / cubrir una brecha)."],["146oe72","Collocation: \"to ___ a limit\"","set / impose / exceed a limit (fijar / imponer / superar un límite)."],["1ugsixj","Collocation: \"to ___ a point\" (make people understand)","make a point / get the point across (dejar claro un argumento)."],["i2fm3k","Collocation: \"to ___ to a conclusion\" (jump to it too quickly)","jump to conclusions (sacar conclusiones precipitadas)."],["liu68v","Collocation: \"on a ___ basis\" (each week)","weekly basis / regular basis / daily basis (con periodicidad semanal / regular / diaria)."],["elhehk","Collocation: \"to be ___ of the fact\" (know about something)","aware of the fact / fully aware (ser plenamente consciente). Adjective \"aware\" takes \"of\"."],["c8z6fc","Collocation: \"___ efforts\" (very hard)","concerted / strenuous / considerable efforts (esfuerzos coordinados / enérgicos)."],["lrifsj","Collocation: \"a ___ decision\" (very difficult)","tough / difficult decision, \"informed decision\" (decisión fundada), \"snap decision\" (decisión precipitada)."],["1rafykw","Collocation: \"to ___ the bar\" (make a standard higher)","raise the bar (elevar el listón)."],["86c7gb","Collocation: \"___ a sigh of relief\"","breathe / heave a sigh of relief (respirar aliviado)."],["ywb0dd","Collocation: \"to ___ light on\" something","shed / throw light on (arrojar luz sobre): \"The report sheds light on the causes of the crash.\""],["kjnxnf","Collocation: \"to ___ the ground\" (start a project fast)","hit the ground running (empezar con fuerza). Also \"get off the ground\" (despegar, ponerse en marcha)."],["koje62","Collocation: \"a ___ of thought\" (a way of thinking)","train of thought (hilo del pensamiento). Also \"school of thought\" (corriente de pensamiento)."],["1ggnme8","Collocation: \"a ___ margin\" (very small)","narrow / slim / tight margin (margen estrecho). \"Safety margin\" (margen de seguridad)."],["h9bqnk","Collocation: \"to ___ compliance with\" a rule","ensure / achieve / demonstrate compliance (with) (garantizar / demostrar el cumplimiento)."],["uoeae8","Collocation: \"to ___ a ban\" (start it)","impose / lift / enforce a ban (imponer / levantar una prohibición)."],["bkpwy","Collocation: \"to ___ suspicion\" (cause it)","arouse / raise suspicion (levantar sospechas)."],["139vs5","Collocation: \"to reach a ___\" (agreement)","reach a consensus / an agreement / a compromise (alcanzar un consenso)."],["1wmipli","Collocation: \"to ___ the odds\" (be successful although it seems unlikely)","beat the odds (superar las expectativas): \"Against all odds...\" (contra todo pronóstico)."],["1c4ai01","Collocation: \"to ___ to good use\"","put to good use (aprovechar bien): \"She put her training to good use.\""],["1f2fgq7","Collocation: \"a ___ of responsibility\"","sense of responsibility (sentido de la responsabilidad). Also \"heavy responsibility\"."],["cy2ca2","Phrasal verb: \"call off\" (an event or plan)","to cancel: \"The flight was called off because of fog.\" (cancelar, suspender)"],["rq0ivk","Phrasal verb: \"carry out\"","to perform or complete a task: \"The engineers carried out an inspection.\" (llevar a cabo)"],["1k40kaq","Phrasal verb: \"come up with\"","to think of an idea or solution: \"She came up with a new procedure.\" (idear, se le ocurre)"],["1eacay9","Phrasal verb: \"cut back on\"","to reduce: \"The airline cut back on short-haul flights.\" (reducir)"],["1gxn743","Phrasal verb: \"deal with\"","to handle or take action about: \"Controllers must deal with unexpected events.\" (ocuparse de, hacer frente a)"],["bsfur8","Phrasal verb: \"drop off\" (two meanings)","1) to fall asleep; 2) to decrease: \"Demand drops off in winter.\" (1: quedarse dormido; 2: disminuir)"],["6o5iuh","Phrasal verb: \"end up\"","to finally be in a situation or place: \"We ended up landing at a different airport.\" (acabar, terminar)"],["ox7ljr","Phrasal verb: \"figure out\"","to understand or solve after thinking: \"It took an hour to figure out the fault.\" (averiguar, descifrar)"],["1f2p8ol","Phrasal verb: \"follow up (on)\"","to take further action about something: \"Please follow up on the incident report.\" (hacer un seguimiento)"],["q47970","Phrasal verb: \"get across\"","to make something understood: \"He could not get his point across.\" (hacerse entender)"],["11pxoev","Phrasal verb: \"get away with\"","to avoid punishment for something wrong: \"You cannot get away with ignoring clearances.\" (salir impune)"],["18qu8vx","Phrasal verb: \"give in\"","to stop resisting and accept: \"The airline gave in to union demands.\" (ceder, rendirse)"],["egbaya","Phrasal verb: \"go through\" (a process or experience)","to experience or examine carefully: \"He went through a difficult period.\" / \"Go through the checklist.\" (pasar por; repasar)"],["1mtpjsu","Phrasal verb: \"hand over\"","to give control or responsibility to someone else: \"She handed over the position at 14:00.\" (traspasar, entregar el relevo)"],["1anww67","Phrasal verb: \"hold up\"","to delay: \"The storm held up all departures.\" (retrasar)"],["c7oreh","Phrasal verb: \"keep up with\"","to stay at the same level or pace as: \"It is hard to keep up with new regulations.\" (mantenerse al día)"],["182a170","Phrasal verb: \"look into\"","to investigate: \"The authority is looking into the incident.\" (investigar)"],["ek6owl","Phrasal verb: \"make up for\"","to compensate for: \"Extra staff made up for the shortage.\" (compensar)"],["1h1lfw8","Phrasal verb: \"pick up\" (speed, or a skill)","to increase: \"Traffic picks up after 07:00.\" / to learn casually: \"pick up a language\" (aumentar; aprender sin esfuerzo)"],["1udnpqn","Phrasal verb: \"point out\"","to draw attention to a fact: \"She pointed out an error in the plan.\" (señalar)"],["1tsbpn1","Phrasal verb: \"pull off\"","to succeed in doing something difficult: \"They pulled off a perfect landing in crosswinds.\" (lograr, conseguir)"],["1oz9p8x","Phrasal verb: \"put off\"","to postpone; or to discourage: \"Do not put off the maintenance.\" (aplazar; desanimar)"],["1fwzf0j","Phrasal verb: \"put up with\"","to tolerate: \"Controllers must put up with noise and pressure.\" (soportar, aguantar)"],["noornx","Phrasal verb: \"run out of\"","to have no more of something: \"The aircraft ran out of fuel.\" (quedarse sin)"],["134ug9e","Phrasal verb: \"set off\"","to start a journey; or to cause an alarm to start: \"The smoke set off the alarm.\" (partir; activar)"],["5rqjmo","Phrasal verb: \"set up\"","to establish or arrange: \"A crisis team was set up.\" (establecer, montar)"],["1sxat8f","Phrasal verb: \"sort out\"","to solve a problem or arrange something: \"We sorted out the confusion.\" (solucionar, arreglar)"],["1dt795o","Phrasal verb: \"stand for\"","to represent or mean; or to tolerate: \"ATC stands for air traffic control.\" / \"I won't stand for it.\" (significar; tolerar)"],["xj0fhh","Phrasal verb: \"stand out\"","to be easily noticeable or better than others: \"Her calm voice stood out.\" (destacar)"],["ay8sjp","Phrasal verb: \"take on\"","to accept a task or employ people: \"The company took on 50 controllers.\" (asumir; contratar)"],["16sang4","Phrasal verb: \"take over\"","to gain control from someone: \"The new team takes over next week.\" (asumir el control, relevar)"],["ueu3xq","Phrasal verb: \"turn down\"","to reject an offer or request; also to reduce volume: \"He turned down the job.\" (rechazar; bajar)"],["p83fyu","Phrasal verb: \"turn out\"","to happen in a particular way, or to prove to be: \"It turned out to be a false alarm.\" (resultar)"],["1088whp","Phrasal verb: \"wear off\"","to gradually disappear: \"The effects of the medication wore off.\" (pasarse, desaparecer)"],["138k320","Phrasal verb: \"work out\"","to calculate or solve; to exercise: \"Work out the fuel needed.\" (calcular; entrenar)"],["ujlxkt","Phrasal verb: \"back up\"","to support or copy data: \"Back up your files. His data backed up the claim.\" (respaldar; hacer copia)"],["125ksr0","Phrasal verb: \"break down\"","to stop working; to divide into parts: \"The radar broke down.\" (averiarse; desglosar)"],["u2ls6u","Phrasal verb: \"bring about\"","to cause something to happen: \"The reform brought about major change.\" (provocar, ocasionar)"],["4h8gvz","Phrasal verb: \"carry on\"","to continue: \"Carry on with the checklist.\" (continuar, seguir)"],["69gzgl","Phrasal verb: \"check in / check out\"","to register on arrival / to leave a hotel or verify something: \"The passengers checked in at 06:00.\" (facturar; salir del hotel)"],["11lm79q","Phrasal verb: \"come across\"","to find by chance, or to give an impression: \"He comes across as calm.\" (encontrarse con; dar la impresión)"],["6e0ke3","Phrasal verb: \"fall through\"","to fail to happen: \"The merger fell through.\" (fracasar, quedar en nada)"],["26f50c","Phrasal verb: \"look up to\"","to admire or respect someone: \"Trainees look up to their instructors.\" (admirar)"],["y0ekjs","Phrasal verb: \"phase out\"","to stop using something gradually: \"Old radar systems are being phased out.\" (retirar progresivamente)"],["asuclp","Phrasal verb: \"rule out\"","to exclude as a possibility: \"Investigators ruled out sabotage.\" (descartar)"],["5xafo0","Phrasal verb: \"touch down\"","to land: \"The aircraft touched down at 11:04.\" (aterrizar, tomar tierra)"],["1atu7dl","Phrasal verb: \"take off\"","1) leave the ground; 2) become successful; 3) remove: \"Sales took off.\" (despegar; despuntar; quitarse)"],["ru22li","Phrasal verb: \"go around\" (aviation)","to abort a landing and climb away: \"The aircraft went around because of a vehicle on the runway.\" (frustrar la aproximación, \"ir y al aire\")"],["g0374u","Idiom: \"the tip of the iceberg\"","only a small visible part of a much bigger problem (la punta del iceberg)."],["3z53zv","Idiom: \"a blessing in disguise\"","something that seems bad but has a good result (una bendición disfrazada)."],["eg8rcn","Idiom: \"to bite the bullet\"","to accept an unpleasant necessity and deal with it bravely (hacer de tripas corazón)."],["1o3nd1c","Idiom: \"to cut corners\"","to do something in the quickest or cheapest way, ignoring rules or quality (escatimar; saltarse pasos). Never acceptable in safety-critical work."],["1cha6te","Idiom: \"to be on the same page\"","to share the same understanding or plan (estar de acuerdo, entenderse)."],["1e2jabo","Idiom: \"the ball is in your court\"","it is your turn to decide or act (te toca actuar a ti)."],["pmhmei","Idiom: \"to call it a day\"","to stop working for the day (dar por terminado el trabajo)."],["1ukl3gx","Idiom: \"a piece of cake\"","something very easy (pan comido)."],["vbcmgo","Idiom: \"under the weather\"","slightly ill (indispuesto, pachucho)."],["473vd","Idiom: \"once in a blue moon\"","very rarely (de uvas a peras, muy de vez en cuando)."],["41uwjc","Idiom: \"to hit the nail on the head\"","to describe exactly what is causing a situation or problem (dar en el clavo)."],["ac1vfa","Idiom: \"to go the extra mile\"","to make more effort than is expected (hacer un esfuerzo extra)."],["nn0cfn","Idiom: \"to keep someone in the loop\"","to keep someone informed (mantener a alguien al corriente)."],["vf2lvc","Idiom: \"back to square one\"","back at the beginning after a failed attempt (volver a empezar desde cero)."],["1enznwg","Idiom: \"to get cold feet\"","to become nervous and hesitate before an important action (echarse atrás por miedo)."],["14o77x3","Idiom: \"to jump on the bandwagon\"","to join an activity that has become popular (subirse al carro)."],["176e3vr","Idiom: \"the last straw\"","the final problem in a series that makes a situation unbearable (la gota que colma el vaso)."],["2h1yrl","Idiom: \"to pull someone's leg\"","to joke by telling someone something untrue (tomar el pelo)."],["1vpu6vk","Idiom: \"to see eye to eye\"","to agree completely (estar totalmente de acuerdo)."],["1b6t06h","Idiom: \"to take something with a pinch of salt\"","to not completely believe something (tomar con cautela / con pinzas)."],["zxylv0","Idiom: \"in the nick of time\"","just before it is too late (justo a tiempo, en el último momento)."],["6cy6jo","Idiom: \"to burn the midnight oil\"","to work late into the night (trabajar hasta altas horas de la noche)."],["m2oihz","Idiom: \"at the drop of a hat\"","immediately, without thinking (sin pensárselo dos veces)."],["11l8dv6","Idiom: \"to be in hot water\"","to be in trouble (estar en un aprieto)."],["1dptlz3","Idiom: \"to miss the boat\"","to lose an opportunity (perder la oportunidad, \"perder el tren\")."],["116zj4q","Idiom: \"by the book\"","strictly following the rules (al pie de la letra, según el reglamento). Very positive in aviation."],["1di8iye","Idiom: \"to play it by ear\"","to improvise without a fixed plan (improvisar sobre la marcha)."],["1xikwk4","Idiom: \"a hot potato\"","a controversial topic that is difficult to handle (un asunto espinoso)."],["qm9sqw","Idiom: \"to spill the beans\"","to reveal a secret (irse de la lengua, destapar el pastel)."],["1o4xih5","Idiom: \"to get the ball rolling\"","to start an activity or process (poner en marcha, echar a rodar)."],["1h80y2y","Idiom: \"in a nutshell\"","in the fewest possible words (en pocas palabras, en resumen)."],["sgc8f9","Idiom: \"to keep a low profile\"","to avoid attracting attention (pasar desapercibido)."],["1oja4ow","Idiom: \"to be up in the air\"","not yet decided, uncertain (estar en el aire, sin decidir)."],["1fx3y1o","Linking device: express CONTRAST between two facts, formal, at the start of a clause (\"The plan is cheap. ___, it is risky.\")","However / Nevertheless / Nonetheless (sin embargo, no obstante). \"Nevertheless\" and \"nonetheless\" are more formal than \"however\"."],["ohr0vk","Linking device: \"whereas\" and \"while\" used to contrast","whereas / while (mientras que): \"Some airports are busy, whereas others are almost empty.\" Compares two things in one sentence."],["1fk4mud","Linking device: \"on the one hand ... on the other hand\" vs \"by contrast\"","Both present opposite points of view. \"On the one hand / on the other hand\" gives two sides of one issue; \"by contrast\" (en cambio) highlights a difference between two separate things."],["m881xa","Linking device: \"in spite of\" / \"despite\": what follows them?","A noun, a pronoun or an -ing form (not a full clause): \"Despite the fog, the flight departed.\" / \"In spite of being tired, she finished.\" With a clause: \"despite the fact that ...\"."],["15u8a32","Linking device: \"although\" / \"even though\" / \"though\": what follows them?","A full clause (subject + verb): \"Although it was foggy, the flight departed.\" \"Even though\" is stronger than \"although\". \"Though\" can also come at the end: \"It was cold, though.\""],["1iewayb","Linking device: ADDITION, formal: \"In ___, the airport needs a new tower.\"","In addition (además) / Moreover / Furthermore (asimismo, por otra parte). \"Moreover\" and \"furthermore\" are formal."],["1pges9w","Linking device: RESULT, formal: \"The engine failed; ___, the crew diverted.\"","consequently / therefore / as a result / hence / thus (por lo tanto, en consecuencia). \"Hence\" and \"thus\" are very formal."],["1czc4mu","Linking device: \"hence\" (meaning and position)","\"Therefore / for this reason\": \"The wind rose; hence the delay.\" Usually followed by a noun phrase (not a full clause)."],["4isny9","Linking device: \"whereby\"","\"By which / according to which\": \"a system whereby all flights are tracked.\" (mediante el cual). Formal."],["fjlqd0","Linking device: \"thereby\" + -ing","\"By that means, as a result\": \"Controllers reduced the speed, thereby increasing separation.\" (con lo cual)"],["ohze57","Linking device: REASON, formal: \"___ the storm, the airport closed.\"","Owing to / Due to / Because of / In view of (debido a, en vista de). \"Owing to\" and \"due to\" are often interchangeable; \"due to\" also follows \"be\"."],["n2kvip","Linking device: \"given that\" / \"in view of the fact that\"","Because of a known fact: \"Given that the runway is wet, we shall reduce the load.\" (dado que)"],["r1rswm","Linking device: \"provided (that)\" / \"as long as\" / \"providing\"","On condition that: \"You may proceed provided that you report established.\" (siempre que)"],["22gl4l","Linking device: \"unless\" (meaning)","\"If ... not / except if\": \"Unless you hear from us, proceed as planned.\" (a menos que). It is already negative: do not add \"not\"."],["18tziyy","Linking device: \"otherwise\" (two uses)","1) \"if not, or else\": \"Report now; otherwise we will assume you are unable.\" 2) \"in other ways\": \"The plan was otherwise perfect.\" (de lo contrario; por lo demás)"],["1mx2a80","Linking device: \"so as to\" / \"in order to\" / \"so that\": which introduces a purpose clause with a subject?","\"so that\" + subject + verb: \"She spoke slowly so that everybody could understand.\" \"So as to / in order to\" + infinitive (para)."],["1w9zg81","Linking device: \"lest\"","Formal/literary: \"in order to prevent\": \"He checked the list lest he forget anything.\" (por temor a que, no fuera a). Followed by subjunctive or \"should\"."],["18htp0e","Linking device: \"admittedly\" and \"granted\"","They concede a point before arguing the opposite: \"Admittedly, the delay was short; still, it was avoidable.\" (es cierto que, sin duda)"],["blc9i9","Linking device: \"that said\" / \"having said that\"","Introduces a contrast after a concession: \"The system is expensive. That said, it saves lives.\" (dicho esto, aun así)"],["155rpv4","Linking device: \"insofar as\" / \"in so far as\"","To the extent that: \"The plan is sound insofar as it reduces risk.\" (en la medida en que)"],["1erjx5u","Linking device: \"as opposed to\"","In contrast with: \"Radar control, as opposed to procedural control, uses surveillance data.\" (a diferencia de, frente a)"],["1x7n8s5","Linking device: \"with regard to\" / \"with reference to\" / \"as regards\"","Formal ways to introduce a topic: \"With regard to your request, ...\" (en cuanto a, con respecto a)"],["3et98w","Linking device: \"notwithstanding\"","Formal: \"despite, in spite of\": \"Notwithstanding the fog, the flights departed.\" Can follow the noun: \"the fog notwithstanding\". (a pesar de)"],["46nxt0","Linking device: \"on the grounds that\" / \"on the basis that\"","Giving the reason for an action or claim: \"The licence was refused on the grounds that the test was failed.\" (basándose en que)"],["plx9qa","Linking device: \"to sum up\" / \"in conclusion\" / \"all things considered\"","Signal the end of a text: (en resumen, en conclusión, considerándolo todo). Use them at the end of an essay."],["1tddmcq","Linking device: \"no sooner ... than\" (structure and word order)","\"No sooner had the aircraft landed than the alarm sounded.\" After \"No sooner\" use inversion (had + subject + past participle). Meaning: as soon as (apenas ... cuando)."],["1nksm6a","Linking device: \"hardly ... when\" / \"scarcely ... when\" (structure)","\"Hardly had he sat down when the phone rang.\" Inversion after a negative adverb at the start. (apenas ... cuando)"],["4rz2cz","Linking device: \"not only ... but also\" with inversion","\"Not only did the pilot land safely, but he also saved the aircraft.\" After \"Not only\" at the start use auxiliary + subject."],["e6o588","Linking device: \"by the same token\"","In the same way; for the same reason: \"Pilots must be alert; by the same token, controllers must be too.\" (del mismo modo)"],["7kpk1e","Linking device: \"whilst\" vs \"while\"","\"Whilst\" is a formal British variant of \"while\" (mientras que; mientras)."],["1jzhc1o","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"buy\"","purchase (adquirir, comprar). \"buy\" is neutral/informal."],["11leqik","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"start\"","commence (comenzar) / initiate. \"start\" and \"begin\" are neutral."],["kiqz05","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"find out\"","ascertain (determinar, cerciorarse): \"The investigators sought to ascertain the cause.\""],["4i44sv","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"ask\" (for information)","enquire / inquire (informarse, preguntar). \"Enquire\" is British; \"inquire\" is US and also used in Britain."],["w0ij6p","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"help\"","assist (asistir, ayudar). Note: \"assist\" in English does not mean \"asistir a un lugar\" (that is \"attend\")."],["v4ghmk","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"need\"","require (requerir)."],["dm3sgk","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"end / stop\"","terminate (terminar, poner fin a)."],["72b6gr","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"show\"","demonstrate (demostrar)."],["14yuhkk","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"enough\"","sufficient (suficiente)."],["8xegps","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"get\" (obtain)","obtain (obtener)."],["10inn3d","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"about\" (topic)","regarding / concerning (con respecto a). \"I am writing regarding your application.\""],["i5w5if","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"try\"","endeavour (esforzarse, procurar; British spelling; US: endeavor)."],["airdsy","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"first\"","initial (inicial)."],["y84j5w","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"later / next\"","subsequent (posterior, subsiguiente)."],["1wh2ix7","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"keep\"","retain (conservar, retener)."],["1ufmbjt","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"before\"","prior to (con anterioridad a, antes de)."],["i030d6","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"after\"","following (tras, a raíz de): \"Following the incident, the runway was closed.\""],["lnzst3","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"tell (inform)\"","inform / notify (comunicar, informar). \"I regret to inform you that ...\" vs \"Sorry to tell you that ...\""],["10lj87v","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"kids\"","children (niños). \"Kids\" is informal, \"offspring\" very formal."],["1281ej4","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"get in touch\"","contact (ponerse en contacto): \"Please contact us if you require further information.\""],["1wuknqi","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"look at\" (examine)","examine / review (examinar, revisar)."],["spwqnk","Register pair: formal equivalent of \"go up\" (increase)","increase / rise (aumentar). \"go up\" is neutral; \"soar\" is stronger."],["164g9h5","Register pair: formal opening of a letter when you do not know the name","\"Dear Sir or Madam,\" (Estimado/a señor/a) ... closing \"Yours faithfully\". Informal: \"Hi,\" / \"Cheers\"."],["1blfof6","Register pair: formal closing when you know the name","\"Dear Ms Green,\" ... \"Yours sincerely,\". US usage: \"Sincerely,\"."],["2atnat","Register pair: informal equivalent of \"children\" or \"mother\" in speech","kids; mum (UK) / mom (US). Formal: children; mother."],["1gejb00","Register pair: informal equivalent of \"purchase\"","buy (comprar). Formal: purchase."],["1apxue6","False friend (Spanish speakers): \"actually\" is NOT \"actualmente\". What does it mean?","\"Actually\" = \"de hecho / en realidad\". \"Actualmente\" = currently / nowadays / at present."],["1tdwzml","False friend: \"eventually\" is NOT \"eventualmente\".","\"Eventually\" = \"finalmente, al final\". \"Eventualmente\" (posiblemente) = possibly / occasionally."],["j3jdzd","False friend: \"sensible\" is NOT \"sensible\".","\"Sensible\" = \"sensato, razonable\". \"Sensible\" (Spanish) = sensitive."],["69q0c0","False friend: \"sympathetic\" is NOT \"simpático\".","\"Sympathetic\" = \"comprensivo, compasivo\". \"Simpático\" = nice / friendly / likeable."],["18rv5x2","False friend: \"to assist\" vs \"asistir\".","\"To assist\" = ayudar. \"Asistir a\" (attend) = to attend. \"Attend\" does not mean \"atender\" (= to serve / to deal with)."],["6jkdth","False friend: \"library\" is NOT \"librería\".","\"Library\" = biblioteca. \"Librería\" = bookshop / bookstore."],["vp73r4","False friend: \"embarrassed\" is NOT \"embarazada\".","\"Embarrassed\" = avergonzado. \"Embarazada\" = pregnant."],["1qcfqf4","False friend: \"to realize\" vs \"realizar\".","\"To realize\" = darse cuenta. \"Realizar\" (carry out) = to carry out / to perform."],["7r9nwc","False friend: \"carpet\" is NOT \"carpeta\".","\"Carpet\" = alfombra, moqueta. \"Carpeta\" = folder."],["1yd8z7z","False friend: \"exit\" is NOT \"éxito\".","\"Exit\" = salida. \"Éxito\" = success."],["nukfcv","False friend: \"large\" is NOT \"largo\".","\"Large\" = grande. \"Largo\" = long."],["nzwk9f","False friend: \"lecture\" is NOT \"lectura\".","\"Lecture\" = conferencia, clase magistral. \"Lectura\" = reading."],["1wr01yf","False friend: \"to pretend\" is NOT \"pretender\".","\"To pretend\" = fingir. \"Pretender\" = to intend / to aim to."],["1xe5twc","False friend: \"to resume\" is NOT \"resumir\".","\"To resume\" = reanudar. \"Resumir\" = to summarize."],["mtox7z","False friend: \"constipated\" is NOT \"constipado\".","\"Constipated\" = estreñido. \"Constipado\" (Spanish) = to have a cold."],["akvfp","False friend: \"educated\" is NOT \"educado\".","\"Educated\" = culto, con estudios. \"Educado\" (polite) = polite / well-mannered."],["dzkep1","False friend: \"fabric\" is NOT \"fábrica\".","\"Fabric\" = tela, tejido. \"Fábrica\" = factory."],["771r9k","False friend: \"notice\" is NOT \"noticia\".","\"Notice\" = aviso, anuncio; also \"to notice\" = darse cuenta. \"Noticia\" = a piece of news."],["1e1uzob","False friend: \"parents\" is NOT \"parientes\".","\"Parents\" = padres. \"Parientes\" = relatives."],["nt3wi0","False friend: \"petrol\" is NOT \"petróleo\".","\"Petrol\" (UK) / \"gas\" (US) = gasolina. \"Petróleo\" = oil / crude oil."],["1k8yyrh","False friend: \"to record\" is NOT \"recordar\".","\"To record\" = grabar, registrar. \"Recordar\" = to remember (or \"to remind\")."],["1e7r0lk","False friend: \"to support\" is NOT \"soportar\" in the sense of \"tolerate\".","\"To support\" = apoyar, respaldar, sostener. \"Soportar\" (tolerate) = to bear / to put up with."],["1gqf3qw","False friend: \"injury\" is NOT \"injuria\".","\"Injury\" = lesión, herida. \"Injuria\" = insult."],["13e44jr","False friend: \"to attend\" is NOT \"atender\".","\"To attend\" = asistir a. \"Atender\" = to serve, to deal with, to look after."],["jxoa1i","False friend: \"disgust\" is NOT \"disgusto\".","\"Disgust\" = asco, repugnancia. \"Disgusto\" = upset / displeasure / annoyance."],["wn5gkl","False friend: \"compromise\" vs \"compromiso\".","\"Compromise\" = acuerdo mutuo con concesiones. \"Compromiso\" = commitment / obligation / engagement."],["a3jwoo","False friend: \"argument\" vs \"argumento\".","\"Argument\" = discusión (a quarrel) or razonamiento (a reasoned case). \"Argumento\" of a film or book = the plot."],["11x414f","False friend: \"to introduce\" and \"presentar\".","\"To introduce\" = presentar a alguien (people); also \"introducir\". \"Presentar un informe\" = to submit a report; \"to present\" = to give a talk."],["1blqni1","False friend: \"rope\" is NOT \"ropa\".","\"Rope\" = cuerda. \"Ropa\" = clothes."],["1fsg7n6","False friend: \"journey\" is NOT \"jornada\".","\"Journey\" = viaje (a trip). \"Jornada\" = working day; \"shift\" (turno)."],["ykatqz","False friend: \"physician\" is NOT \"físico\".","\"Physician\" = médico. \"Físico\" = physicist / physical."],["ghkr8s","False friend: \"to retire\" is NOT \"retirar\".","\"To retire\" = jubilarse (or retirarse a descansar). \"Retirar\" (withdraw) = to withdraw / to remove."],["af7lxt","False friend: \"to demand\" is NOT \"demandar\".","\"To demand\" = exigir. \"Demandar\" (sue) = to sue."],["2q5smu","False friend: \"success\" vs \"suceso\".","\"Success\" = éxito. \"Suceso\" = event / incident / occurrence."],["it6xd","False friend: \"to molest\" is NOT \"molestar\".","\"To molest\" = acosar sexualmente / abusar. \"Molestar\" (annoy) = to bother / to annoy."],["3vvh7u","False friend: \"audience\" is NOT \"audiencia\" (court).","\"Audience\" = público. \"Audiencia\" (court hearing) = hearing / court."],["btie1a","False friend: \"assume\" and \"asumir\".","\"To assume\" = suponer. \"Asumir\" (take on responsibility) = to take on / to accept."],["q3e8nq","False friend: \"commodity\" is NOT \"comodidad\".","\"Commodity\" = materia prima, producto básico. \"Comodidad\" = comfort."],["15mz1jj","Preposition: \"depend ___\" (Spanish \"depender de\")","depend on: \"It depends on the weather.\" (depender de) Not \"depend of\"."],["wwlbxd","Preposition: \"consist ___\"","consist of: \"The exam consists of two parts.\" (consistir en)"],["1ta86ie","Preposition: \"responsible ___ safety\"","responsible for (responsable de): \"He is responsible for the runway.\""],["gca4kf","Preposition: \"interested ___\"","interested in (interesado en)."],["jsofi0","Preposition: \"good ___ maths\"","good at (bueno en): \"She is good at mental arithmetic.\""],["itjpxn","Preposition: \"afraid ___\"","afraid of (miedo de): \"He is afraid of heights.\""],["16hb1cv","Preposition: \"different ___\"","different from (British: also \"different to\"; US also \"different than\"): (distinto de)."],["174mi5c","Preposition: \"capable ___\"","capable of (capaz de) + -ing: \"capable of landing in fog.\""],["1yo142","Preposition: \"insist ___\"","insist on (insistir en) + noun/-ing: \"He insisted on reading it back.\""],["1q8jm9a","Preposition: \"result ___\" (cause an effect) vs \"result ___\" (be the effect)","result in (dar lugar a): \"The error resulted in a delay.\" Result from (deberse a): \"The delay resulted from the error.\""],["1onev47","Preposition: \"contribute ___\"","contribute to (contribuir a): \"Fatigue contributed to the accident.\""],["11ucrxj","Preposition: \"in charge ___\"","in charge of (a cargo de): \"He is in charge of the shift.\""],["1fjkcfl","Preposition: \"at the age ___\"","at the age of (a la edad de)."],["1rjh3gd","Preposition: \"by ___ / on ___\" (not deliberately vs deliberately)","by mistake (por error) / on purpose (a propósito, adrede)."],["130l55i","Preposition: \"in time\" vs \"on time\"","\"In time\" = with enough time to spare: \"in time to catch the flight\". \"On time\" = at the scheduled time (puntual): \"The flight departed on time.\""],["wdpp74","Preposition: \"at the end\" vs \"in the end\"","\"At the end (of)\" = at the last point: \"at the end of the runway\". \"In the end\" = finally (al final): \"In the end, they diverted.\""],["1j19zq1","Preposition: \"arrive ___\" a city / a small place","arrive in a city or country; arrive at a small place or building: \"arrive in Madrid\", \"arrive at the airport\". (llegar a)"],["1o3etro","Preposition: \"at ___ / on ___ / in ___\" with days, dates, months","on Monday, on 5 May; in May, in 2027; at 06:00. (a los días: on; a los meses y años: in; a las horas: at)"],["1psvwau","Preposition: \"in / at / on\" with the place of a flight","on a plane / on a bus / on a train (a bordo), but in a car / in a taxi."],["gu21so","Preposition: \"agree ___ someone / agree ___ a plan\"","agree with someone; agree on a plan (or \"agree to\" a proposal): \"I agree with you.\" (estar de acuerdo con)"],["bmi106","Preposition: \"apologize ___ something\"","apologize for something / to someone: \"He apologized for the delay.\" (disculparse por)"],["3oi0xa","Preposition: \"accuse someone ___\"","accuse someone of: \"She was accused of negligence.\" (acusar de)"],["121m2tx","Preposition: \"believe ___\" (trust) vs \"believe\" (accept that it is true)","believe in (creer en: have faith in); believe someone / something (creer que lo que dice es verdad)."],["xx0mqs","Preposition: \"look forward ___\"","look forward to + -ing / noun (tener ganas de): \"I look forward to hearing from you.\""],["119zcqg","Preposition: \"according ___\"","according to (según): \"According to the forecast, the wind will drop.\" Not \"according with\"."],["10ftzst","Preposition: \"prefer X ___ Y\"","prefer X to Y: \"I prefer flying to driving.\" (preferir X a Y). Not \"than\"."],["1y39glg","Preposition: \"suffer ___ an illness\"","suffer from: \"He suffers from hay fever.\" (padecer)"],["14z81ft","Preposition: \"the reason ___ the delay\"","the reason for (la razón de): \"the reason for the delay.\""],["js5x","Preposition: \"worried ___ / anxious ___\"","worried about (preocupado por); anxious about / for."],["16px689","Preposition: \"the difference ___ two things\"","the difference between two things: \"the difference between QNH and QFE.\" (la diferencia entre)"],["1ny5ebw","Preposition: \"the solution ___ a problem\"","the solution to a problem (la solución a). Not \"of\"."],["1jy4dr2","Preposition: \"increase ___ 5%\" vs \"increase ___ 5%\"","increase by 5% (the amount of change); increase to 5% (the final level). Also \"an increase of 5%\"."],["11i22qm","Preposition: \"aware ___ / conscious ___\"","aware of / conscious of (consciente de)."],["1kd44zf","Preposition: \"similar ___\"","similar to (parecido a)."],["103v9kc","Preposition: \"involved ___\" (participating in)","involved in (implicado en, participar en): \"involved in an incident\"."]]);
